#!/bin/sh
# Saves the dropbear host keys to ssh/ on the settings partition so that they
# survive a reboot. Only while /settings is mounted, that is from
# otopi-read-settings: afterwards the computer on the USB port may have the
# partition mounted.
set -e
grep -q " /settings " /proc/mounts || { echo "/settings is not mounted" >&2; exit 1; }
mount -o remount,rw /settings
trap 'sync; mount -o remount,ro /settings' EXIT
mkdir -p /settings/ssh
cp /etc/dropbear/dropbear_*_host_key /settings/ssh/
echo "host keys saved to /settings/ssh"
